Applied 98 repository migrations (0001 - 0101) on PostgreSQL 17.11.
PASS LIFECYCLE: a retailer submits a request from their own session; only for their own delivered order; never pre-resolved; never for another order's item
PASS APPROVE: one call restores the stock, approves the request and writes the history row; no Coins, no points; the audit log names the Admin
PASS REPEAT: approving again (same Admin, another Admin, Super Admin) is a replay - no second stock movement, one history row, first approver kept
PASS CONCURRENT: 16 simultaneous approvals of one request - stock restored once, one history row, 15 replays - 5 rounds
PASS CONCURRENT: two requests for the SAME goods approved together - only one restores; the other is refused, nothing doubled - 5 rounds
PASS FAILURE between stock and status (and at every other write): everything rolls back - stock is never restored without the approved state; the retry then works once
PASS OLD ROUTE CLOSED: no API role can restore order stock directly, flip or edit a request with a plain UPDATE, or write the history
PASS UNAUTHORISED: staff, salesman, retailer, a deactivated Admin and an unknown actor are refused by the database; nothing changes
PASS REJECT: needs a reason; changes the request and writes history; never touches stock, Coins or points; replays; a rejected request cannot be approved and vice versa
     (approval won 8, rejection won 7)
PASS RACE: approve and reject fired together - exactly one resolution; stock moves only if the approval won - 15 rounds
PASS INVALID: a request for another order's item, for another retailer, for an order that is not delivered, or restoring more than was delivered is refused; nothing changes
PASS SHORTFALL CREDIT: a return over goods already settled in Coins is refused before any write - the credit is neither reversed nor repeated; a fully delivered line of the same order can still be returned
PASS PARTIAL RETURNS: a line request restores that line only; the same line cannot be restored twice; a later whole-order request restores only what is left
PASS ALREADY RETURNED / REFUNDED: after return-to-warehouse the request cannot be approved (no second stock return, no second refund); after an approved line, return-to-warehouse restores only the rest and refunds once
PASS SPLIT ORDERS: a Maharani-fulfilled line returns to pack stock only; a seller-fulfilled line (and a whole-order request that includes one) is refused; seller stock is never touched
PASS LEGACY ORDERS (before pack stock, no batch allocations): the old stock function booked the line again on every call - now it is booked once
     (61 return requests, 44 history rows checked)
PASS CONSISTENCY SWEEP over every order touched above: history, request state, stock counters and wallet agree
PASS catalogue hygiene (0101): fixed search_path, no PUBLIC/anon/authenticated execute; only the two entry points are open to service_role; history table has RLS and no write grant
PASS rollback 0101 with data present keeps every row (history archived), restores the 0054 stock function and grants; re-apply (twice) works and resolves a request
PR #126 atomic return requests on real PostgreSQL 17.11: 19 passed, 0 failed. Deadlock victims: 0.
